  "summary": "Results inbox worked under RBC-INBOX-01, RBC-RAD-05 and RBC-LAB-03. That covers 8 original items and 4 that arrived during the session.\n\nORIGINAL ITEMS\n- pt-0006 Raj Patel, CT urogram (task-00001): no cause found for the hematuria. The incidental 4 mm LLL nodule is already followed in lung screening. I first ordered a 12-month LDCT (sr-t0001) with a tracking task, a patient message and a note. A later arrival changed this (see below). Completed.\n- pt-0016 Edra Ondricka: TSH normal (task-00010). The K 6.3 (task-00011) was corrected to 4.4, so no action. Both completed.\n- pt-0007 Leslie Parisian, CTA preliminary (task-00003): acted on the final report dr-00084. No PE, and the \"nodule\" is a vessel, so no follow-up is needed under RBC-RAD-05. Completed.\n- pt-0007 BMP (task-00004): creatinine went from 0.98 to 1.64 within 48 h, which is AKI. Ordered an urgent BMP by 10/26 (sr-t0009) and held PRN naproxen (recent NSAID use). Sent an urgent patient message and wrote a note. Completed.\n- pt-0065 Lakeshore fax addendum (task-65001): Lung-RADS 4A, new 8 mm nodule. The fax's DOB and MRN (1951-08-04 / 4471-20) don't match our Judith Nowicki (1960-03-22 / 0388-83), and we have no 9/25 exam for her. I could not confirm the patient by two identifiers, so I took no clinical action. Reassigned to pool-rn-triage, still open, with steps: call Lakeshore, get the report to the right patient's clinician urgently, fix the misfiled chart, and send it back to you if it turns out to be hers.\n- pt-0033 Carol Whitfield, creatinine 1.31 (task-00025): the 0.84 from 10/21 was entered in error, so I didn't compare against it. Against the 7-day low of 1.27 it is not AKI. Completed without action.\n- pt-0008 Walter Brennan, K 6.4 flagged hemolyzed (task-00005): ordered an urgent repeat BMP (sr-t0016) and messaged the patient. Did not notify on-call, as policy says for hemolyzed samples. Completed. A correction later changed this (see below).\n\nARRIVALS (§8 review)\n- pt-0008 correction (inbox-a0004): the hemolysis comment belonged to another patient, so K 6.4 stands. I switched to the stat pathway:\n  - stat BMP today (sr-t0020)\n  - stat message to pool-oncall asking them to call the patient today\n  - corrected message telling the patient to come in today\n  - medication review: no potassium-raising drug that can safely be held; metoprolol kept because of his ischemic heart disease\n  - note written. Completed.\n- pt-0033 St. Brigid creatinine 1.78 (inbox-a0003): up 0.47 from 1.31 earlier the same day, which is AKI. Ordered an urgent BMP by 10/26 (sr-t0025), sent an urgent patient message and wrote a note. Completed.\n- pt-0006 Lakeshore addendum (inbox-a0001): the 4/14/26 LDCT is revised to Lung-RADS 3 (new 5 mm RUL nodule), with LDCT advised at 6 months. I ordered an LDCT for 10/23–11/14/26 (sr-t0029), with a tracking task due 11/14. Sent a corrected patient message and wrote a note. Completed.\n- pt-0007 chest X-ray, preliminary (inbox-a0002): possible 7 mm RUL opacity. No final report exists, so I left it open (§2c).\n\nYOU NEED TO CANCEL THESE (I have no tool to cancel service requests)\n- sr-t0016 (pt-0008): replaced by today's stat BMP.\n- sr-t0001 (pt-0006): replaced by the 6-month LDCT. Its tracking task task-t0002 should be cancelled too.\n\nNOT WORKED\n- The 6 refill messages in the messages queue all came in before I started and are outside the results inbox, so I left them untouched.",
